"On the SAL boat, Will, an A-rank Shaper who could feel chaos, killed the captain and a thief."
"He steered the Submerger toward Matadero, then injected himself with a potion and slumped."
"At 12:27 AM the boat struck Matadero's shield faster than any submarine on Earth, and was repelled."
"A Wrightmade bomb aboard exploded; the thousand-year-old Sinker Sender blasted apart."
"The cube held firm and nobody at Matadero was harmed; the fighters kept to the site."
"The device's motes raced to Anesidora, causing oceanic anomalies: forced submersion and floods."
"The chaos siren sounded; alerts warned of tsunami-like water and a low chance of chaos exposure."
"The ocean tried to swallow The Span; Nilama Marina and F's family neighborhoods flooded badly."
"Nonessential Contract services on Earth halted, and Anesidora's teleport allotment was raised."
"Artonans quietly began the first stages of a planetary evacuation."
"Burglars looted empty wizards' property; one stole an escape flyer from the Ambassador's residence."
"Wizards blamed humans misdirecting the Sinker Sender, and a reversal-based shield."
"The Contract said the plan formed only at the last moment, not when the boat set out."
"Emergency orders summoned Avowed such as Skiff from Chicago to rescue people in flooded F."
"Rioters tried to force their way into Bunker Street, one of Anesidora's few chaos-rated shelters."
"Chaos exposure was later declared negligible; very few died because Earth's Contract is healthy."
"Just under three hundred died, mostly those refusing evacuation or caught at the sudden start."
"Aulia Velra confessed the Submerger was hers; Orpheus Velra stole and sold it, remembering nothing."
"Aulia claimed a hidden mastermind was behind it and that she may have been the target."
"Emergency domes filled campus greens afterward, and 'Anesidoran Forever' became a slogan."
"A single knight froze a mountain of floodwater against the dawn sky, saving tens of thousands."
"Maricel Alcantara warned the SkySea Guard beforehand, but the Guard failed to find the boat."
"Mina, a high-school Sway stowaway, was the boat's lone survivor, cooperating with authorities."
"She lived because her Fragile Atmosphere was stronger and longer-lasting than the Contract required."
"SAL was blamed; the dead Jacob Moore's father was a Presixter."
"An S-rank Sway offshore heard a mind on the sunken boat, so the System knew seconds before."
"The government kept his role quiet; the female Artonan general thanked him twice."
